IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`

-- Old Age Security Act, "Related Provisions": the transitional and special provisions of other Acts that bear on this one (2007, c. 11, ss 37 and 38;
-- 2010, c. 12, ss 1828 to 1830; 2012, c. 19, s 262; 2021, c. 23, s 275). Section 1830 (the meaning of two terms in an Agreement the text does not reproduce) is inert;
-- see NOTES.md, "Coverage table".
-- The text does not give the day this Act received royal assent in 2007, nor the day on which section 1828 of 2010, c. 12 came into force, so each is an input.
-- Hohfeld: the continued application of the old text (2007 ss 37, 38; 2012 s 262) is an immunity of the person against a change of the rules that bind them (the
-- legislature's disability to apply the new text to them); 2010 s 1829 is an immunity of the officials and of those paid from a finding that their actions were unlawful;
-- 2021 s 275 is a power of the Minister to pay out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund, with no right given to the pensioner.

§ `Related Provisions`

-- 2007, c. 11, s 37: the old subparagraphs 11(7)(e)(ii), 19(6)(d)(ii) and 21(9)(c)(ii) continue to apply to a person who, before the day of royal assent, is a beneficiary of a
-- supplement or an allowance, or has applied for one.
-- src:1150 | 37 Subparagraphs 11(7)(e)(ii), 19(6)(d)(ii) and 21(9)(c)(ii) of the Old Age Security Act, as they read immediately before the day on which this Act receives royal assent, continue to apply to any person who, before that day, is a beneficiary of a supplement or an allowance under that Act or has made an application for payment of a supplement or an allowance under that Act.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, 2007, c. 11, s 37 (src:1150)
GIVEN `before the day on which the 2007 Act receives royal assent, the person is a beneficiary of a supplement or an allowance under the Old Age Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `before that day, the person has made an application for payment of a supplement or an allowance under the Old Age Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`2007, c. 11, s. 37: subparagraphs 11(7)(e)(ii), 19(6)(d)(ii) and 21(9)(c)(ii), as they read immediately before royal assent, continue to apply to the person` `before the day on which the 2007 Act receives royal assent, the person is a beneficiary of a supplement or an allowance under the Old Age Security Act` `before that day, the person has made an application for payment of a supplement or an allowance under the Old Age Security Act` MEANS
        `before the day on which the 2007 Act receives royal assent, the person is a beneficiary of a supplement or an allowance under the Old Age Security Act`
    OR  `before that day, the person has made an application for payment of a supplement or an allowance under the Old Age Security Act`

-- 2007, c. 11, s 38: section 29 as it read before royal assent continues to apply to an application made under it before that day.
-- src:1154 | 38 Section 29 of the Old Age Security Act, as it read immediately before the day on which this Act receives royal assent, continues to apply in respect of any application made under that section before that day.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, 2007, c. 11, s 38 (src:1154)
GIVEN `the application was made under section 29 before the day on which the 2007 Act receives royal assent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`2007, c. 11, s. 38: section 29, as it read immediately before royal assent, continues to apply in respect of the application` `the application was made under section 29 before the day on which the 2007 Act receives royal assent` MEANS
    `the application was made under section 29 before the day on which the 2007 Act receives royal assent`

-- 2010, c. 12, s 1828: "Despite sections 41 and 42 ... the Agreement on Social Security between Canada and the Republic of Poland, signed on April 2, 2008, is deemed to have come
-- into force in Canada on October 1, 2009."
-- src:1158 | 1828 Despite sections 41 and 42 of the Old Age Security Act, the Agreement on Social Security between Canada and the Republic of Poland, signed on April 2, 2008, is deemed to have come into force in Canada on October 1, 2009.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, 2010, c. 12, s 1828 (src:1158)
`2010, c. 12, s. 1828: the day on which the Agreement with the Republic of Poland is deemed to have come into force in Canada` MEANS YearMonthDay 2009 10 1

-- src:1158 | 1828 Despite sections 41 and 42 of the Old Age Security Act, the Agreement on Social Security between Canada and the Republic of Poland, signed on April 2, 2008, is deemed to have come into force in Canada on October 1, 2009.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, 2010, c. 12, s 1828 (src:1158)
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`2010, c. 12, s. 1828: the Agreement with the Republic of Poland is deemed to have been in force in Canada on the day` `the day` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST `2010, c. 12, s. 1828: the day on which the Agreement with the Republic of Poland is deemed to have come into force in Canada`

-- 2010, c. 12, s 1829: all actions taken in accordance with the Agreement's conditions from October 1, 2009 to the day section 1828 comes into force, including the exchange of
-- information and the payment of benefits purporting to have been made under the Act, are deemed lawful.
-- src:1162 | 1829 All actions taken in accordance with the conditions of the Agreement referred to in section 1828 during the period beginning on October 1, 2009 and ending on the day on which section 1828 comes into force, including the exchange of information — with respect to a person — that is obtained under the Old Age Security Act or prepared under that Act from that information between the competent authorities or competent institutions of Canada and the Republic of Poland and the payment of any benefits purporting to have been made under that Act, are deemed to be lawful.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, 2010, c. 12, s 1829 (src:1162)
GIVEN `the action is taken in accordance with the conditions of the Agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the action is taken` IS A DATE
      `the day on which section 1828 comes into force` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`2010, c. 12, s. 1829: the action is deemed to be lawful` `the action is taken in accordance with the conditions of the Agreement` `the day on which the action is taken` `the day on which section 1828 comes into force` MEANS
        `the action is taken in accordance with the conditions of the Agreement`
    AND `the day on which the action is taken` AT LEAST `2010, c. 12, s. 1828: the day on which the Agreement with the Republic of Poland is deemed to have come into force in Canada`
    AND `the day on which the action is taken` AT MOST `the day on which section 1828 comes into force`

-- 2012, c. 19, s 262: the repealed provisions continue to apply to appeals of which a Review Tribunal or the Pension Appeals Board remains seized.
-- src:1170 | 262 The provisions of the Canada Pension Plan and the Old Age Security Act repealed by this Act, and their related regulations, continue to apply to appeals of which a Review Tribunal or the Pension Appeals Board remains seized under this Act, with any necessary adaptations.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, 2012, c. 19, s 262 (src:1170)
GIVEN `a Review Tribunal or the Pension Appeals Board remains seized of the appeal under the 2012 Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`2012, c. 19, s. 262: the repealed provisions of the Canada Pension Plan and the Old Age Security Act, and their related regulations, continue to apply to the appeal` `a Review Tribunal or the Pension Appeals Board remains seized of the appeal under the 2012 Act` MEANS
    `a Review Tribunal or the Pension Appeals Board remains seized of the appeal under the 2012 Act`

-- 2021, c. 23, s 275: any amount payable by the Minister to pensioners who are or will be 75 or older on June 30, 2022, in relation to a program to provide a one-time payment of $500,
-- may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund. The program is not in the text, so the rule gives only the amount that may be so paid; it gives no entitlement.
-- src:1174 | 275 Any amount payable by the Minister of Employment and Social Development to pensioners, as defined in section 2 of the Old Age Security Act, who are or will be 75 years of age or older on June 30, 2022, in relation to a program to provide a one-time payment of $500 to those pensioners, may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, 2021, c. 23, s 275 (src:1174)
GIVEN `the person is a pensioner, as defined in section 2 of the Old Age Security Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`2021, c. 23, s. 275: the amount of the one-time payment to the pensioner that may be paid out of the Consolidated Revenue Fund` `the person is a pensioner, as defined in section 2 of the Old Age Security Act` `the person's date of birth` MEANS
    IF     `the person is a pensioner, as defined in section 2 of the Old Age Security Act`
       AND (`the age in complete years on` (YearMonthDay 2022 6 30) `of a person born on` `the person's date of birth`) AT LEAST 75
    THEN JUST 500
    ELSE NOTHING
